d that this is what  he had to do in order to save his  own people aaron understands reiner now  because aaron  is in a very similar position marlee and  the other nations are about to declare  war on paradise  they are about to attack the island  again and that means that they are going  to try and kill  everyone that aaron ever loved and cared  about  even though there are definitely good  people and innocent people here in  liberio and  all over marley the people in charge are  about to destroy aaron's loved ones  unless he stops them this is the same  predicament that reiner thought that he  was in  back when he attacked paradise it may  not have been true  but that is what he believed and that is  what drove him to keep moving forward  with his mission  but to reiner's credit he doesn't just  blame all his actions  on his environment he says that yes his  environment did play a part  but he also takes personal  responsibility for his decision to  attack  parodies he admits that beyond just the  marlin propaganda  he genuinely wanted to be a hero and he  wanted to be a respected warrior  that is why he convinced annie and  bertolt to continue on with the mission  even after they wanted to give up and  head back to marley  reiner now feels an incredible amount of  guilt about what he did on paradise  and he feels that guilt personally he  doesn't just blame marley he doesn't  just blame brainwashing he blames  himself for choosing to go along with  all of it just so he could be accepted  and respected by marlene society  reiner is so overcome by guilt that he  actually asks aaron to just kill him  and put him out of his misery reiner can  no longer  live with his guilt and even though  reiner knows that aaron is probably  about to go ham on liberio and you would  think that reiner's first instinct would  be to protect liberio  reiner is so broken that he doesn't even  have the will to fight  aaron he simply gives up because he  feels that death at the hands of aa